Vita: --vita-fast-mtx (with patches/aurora/0022). J3DMtxBuffer::calcWeightEnvelopeMtx keeps each
envelope's weighted sum in a local matrix and stores it once, instead of reading and writing the
output matrix on every mix (the compiler cannot keep it in registers: the output may alias). Same
additions, same order, same 0.0f start, same scale flags: the same result bit for bit. On: the local
loop instead of the original; verify: the original writes what the game uses, then each envelope is
summed again locally and compared (counts under the "mtx" switch). Off: one integer test. No game
behaviour changes.

